  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (new TCA Title 39, Chapter 17, Part 13(b)): Except as otherwise provided by state law, the general assembly preempts the entire field of legislation regarding extreme risk protection orders to the exclusion of all county, city, town, municipality, or metropolitan government law, ordinances, resolutions, enactments, or regulation.\nSECTION 1 (new TCA Title 39, Chapter 17, Part 13(c)): A political subdivision of this state is prohibited from accepting a grant or other source of funding for the purpose of implementing an ordinance, rule, executive order, judicial order, or judicial finding that would have the effect of enforcing an extreme risk protection order against a resident of this state."
